$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Chlorination of Heterocycles Gram-scale
Standard Procedure: To a solution of heterocycle (1 g, 1.0 equiv.) in
chloroform (0.1 M) or acetonitrile (0.1 M) at r.t. was added CBMG (1.1
equiv.) with stirring. The reaction was monitored by thin layer
chromatography until completion. Upon consumption of starting material,
the reaction was concentrated under reduced pressure and re-dissolved in
acetonitrile (0.1 M) then filtered using a fritted funnel. The solid left
behind was washed over with cold (0 °C) acetonitrile (0.2 M) until
determined pure by 1H-NMR analysis. 4-chloro-1-phenyl-1H-pyrazole (17).
Gram-scale procedure was followed using 1.1 equiv. of CBMG in
acetonitrile. ethyl 3-chloro-1H-indole-2-carboxylate (22). Gram-scale
standard procedure was followed using 1.1 equiv. of CBMG in chloroform.
22 in 99% yield as a yellow solid. m.p.: 148-149 °C; R f = 0.35 (15%
ethyl ether/hexanes); 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.06 (brs, 1H), 7.72 (d,
J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.38 (d, J = 5.7 Hz, 2H), 7.22 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 1H), 4.47
(q, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H,), 1.46 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H) ppm; 13C-NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 161.2, 134.9, 126.7, 126.4, 122.5, 121.4, 120.4, 112.6, 112.2,
61.6, 14.5 ppm; IR (neat) ν = 3295, 1684, 1520, 1257, 743, 670 cm-1; HRMS
(ESI-TOF) calc’d for C11H10ClNO2 + [M+H] 224.0473; found 224.0475.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, recyclable reagent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
