$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Experimental Procedure11 To a solution of NBS (10.0 mmol, 1.78 g)
in CH2Cl2 (80.0 mL) cooled to -78 °C was added ZrCl4 (0.5 mmol, 116.5
mg), followed by anisole (10.0 mmol, 1.10 mL) under nitrogen atmosphere.
The reaction was stirred for 5 h and then quenched by sat. NaHCO3 aq
solution. The extracted organic phase (CH2Cl2) was washed with brine and
dried over NaSO4. The solvent was removed under reduced pressure to give
as sole product. No further purification is necessary. P-bromoanisole,
yield (1.82 g) 98%. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.37 (m, 2 H), 6.78 (m,
2 H), 3.77 (s, 3 H).
