$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Chlorination of Heterocycles Gram-scale Standard Procedure: To a solution
of heterocycle (1 g, 1.0 equiv.) in chloroform (0.1 M) or acetonitrile
(0.1 M) at r.t. was added CBMG (1.1 equiv.) with stirring. The reaction
was monitored by thin layer chromatography until completion. Upon
consumption of starting material, the reaction was concentrated under
reduced pressure and re-dissolved in acetonitrile (0.1 M) then filtered
using a fritted funnel. The solid left behind was washed over with cold
(0 °C) acetonitrile (0.2 M) until determined pure by 1H-NMR analysis.
4-chloro-1-phenyl-1H-pyrazole (17). Gram-scale procedure was followed
using 1.1 equiv. of CBMG in acetonitrile. 17 in 95% yield as a white
solid. m.p.: 63-65 °C; R f = 0.60 (15% ethyl acetate/hexanes); 1H-NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.90 (s, 1H), 7.66-7.61 (m, 3H), 7.49-7.43 (m, 2H),
7.31 (tt, J = 7.0, 1.0 Hz, 1H) ppm; 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 139.9,
139.6, 129.7, 127.1, 124.9, 119.1, 112.5 ppm; IR (neat) ν = 3115, 1501,
754, 686 cm-1; HRMS (ESI-TOF) calc’d for C9H8ClN+ [M+H] 179.0376; found
179.0372.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, recyclable reagent
