$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure of Halogenations of Pyrazoles in H2O A mixture of
appropriate pyrazole (4 mmol) and NXS (see Table 1 and Table 2) in H2O (5
mL) was stirred at appropriate temperature and time. The progress of the
reaction was monitored by TLC or the 1H NMR spectra of the product (the
disappearance of the signal of the CH of the pyrazole ring). For oily and
water-soluble solid products, the reaction mixture was extracted with
CCl4 (2 x 5 mL) and the extract was dried with MgSO4. The solvent was
removed under reduced pressure. The 4-halopyrazoles were obtained in good
purity as indicated by 1H NMR spectra. For other solid products, the
precipitate was collected by filtration, washed with water (2 x 8 mL),
and dried in air. The products so obtained were in good purity as
indicated by 1H NMR spectra. The samples for elemental analysis were
purified by recrystallizing from appropriate solvents (for the solid
samples) or by column chromatography (for the liquid samples). 2a:
Colorless crystals, yield 98% mp:98-100°C (lit.:[17] 96-97°C). 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.53 (s, 2H, CH), 10.10 (s, 1H, NH).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Halogenation of pyrazoles using N-halosuccinimides in CCl4 and in water
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhao, Zhi-Gang; Wang, Zhong-Xia
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2007), 37(1), 137-147

