$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure of Halogenations of
Pyrazoles in H2O A mixture of appropriate pyrazole (4 mmol) and NXS (see
Table 1 and Table 2) in H2O (5 mL) was stirred at appropriate temperature
and time. The progress of the reaction was monitored by TLC or the 1H NMR
spectra of the product (the disappearance of the signal of the CH of the
pyrazole ring). For oily and water-soluble solid products, the reaction
mixture was extracted with CCl4 (2 x 5 mL) and the extract was dried with
MgSO4. The solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The
4-halopyrazoles were obtained in good purity as indicated by 1H NMR
spectra. For other solid products, the precipitate was collected by
filtration, washed with water (2 x 8 mL), and dried in air. The products
so obtained were in good purity as indicated by 1H NMR spectra. The
samples for elemental analysis were purified by recrystallizing from
appropriate solvents (for the solid samples) or by column chromatography
(for the liquid samples). 3f: Yellow orange oil, yield 97% Anal. calc.
for C12H13ClN2: C, 65.31%; H, 5.94%; N, 12.69%; found: C, 65.69%; H,
5.56%; N, 12.34%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.97 (s, 6H, CH3), 2.21 (s,
3H, CH3), 7.09-7.30 (m, 4H, C6H4). 13C NMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3): δ 9.83,
11.49, 17.28, 108.27, 126.67, 127.87, 129.38, 131.07, 136.18, 136.66,
138.61, 145.57. IR (KBr): ν (cm-1) 3062w, 3030w, 2957m, 2925m, 2860w,
1607w, 1585w, 1558m, 1504vs, 1473m, 1381m, 1293w, 1272w, 1097s, 1032m,
985w, 945w, 818w, 779m, 763s, 722m.
