spectra. For other solid products, the precipitate was collected by
filtration, washed with water (2 x 8 mL), and dried in air. The products
so obtained were in good purity as indicated by 1H NMR spectra. The
samples for elemental analysis were purified by recrystallizing from
appropriate solvents (for the solid samples) or by column chromatography
(for the liquid samples). 3i: White solid, yield 97% mp: 54-55°C. Anal.
calc. for C12H11ClN2O: C, 61.42%; H, 4.72%; N, 11.94%; found: C, 61.18%;
H, 4.73%; N, 12.01%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 2.19 (s, 3H, CH3), 2.56
(s, 3H, CH3), 7.37-7.42 (m, 2H, Ph), 7.48-7.53 (m, 1H, Ph), 7.88 (d, 2H,
J = 7.8 Hz, Ph). 13C NMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3): δ 11.87, 12.41, 114.94,
128.03, 131.48, 132.64, 132.80, 140.43, 149.61, 167.96. IR (KBr): ν
(cm-1) 3069w, 3032w, 2974w, 2931w, 1702vs, 1600m, 1583m, 1490s, 1449s,
1407s, 1378vs, 1343vs, 1276vs, 1206m, 1182m, 1135w, 1084s, 1103w, 1011m,
990s, 935s, 797m, 782m, 712s, 686vs, 624m.
