$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 2 To a solution of 2-fluoro-3-(4-iodo-1H-pyrazol-1-yl)propan-1-ol
(Enantiomer A from compound 66, step 2 above) (770 mg, 2.85 mmol) in DCM
(20 mL) at 0 °C was added methanesulfonyl chloride (0.333 mL, 4.28 mmol)
and triethylamine (0.795 mL, 5.70 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred
for 1 h, then diluted in EtOAc and washed with H2O. The organic layer was
separated and dried over MgSO4. The solution was filtered and
concentrated in vacuo, then purified by flash column chromatography
(0-100% EtOAc/Hexanes gradient) to give 950 mg of
2-fluoro-3-(4-iodo-1H-pyrazol-1-yl)propyl methanesulfonate (96%). LRMS
(ESI) calc’d for (C7H11FIN2O3S) [M+ H]+, 349.0; found 348.9.
