$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-hydroxybenzoyl-N-[(5-bromo-4-phenyl)thiazol-2-yl)amide (26). A solution
of N-bromosuccinimide (4.04 g, 22.7 mmol) in CHCl3 (200 mL) was added
over 45 min to a solution of 2-amino-4-phenylthiazole (4.00 g, 22.7 mmol)
in CHCl3 (200 mL). After 1 h, the reaction was concentrated in vacuo,
then the residue was suspended in conc. aq. NH3 (100 mL) and filtered.
The white solid formed was washed with H2O (2×), dissolved in CH2Cl2,
washed with brine, dried and evaporated, which was sufficiently pure to
use directly. 2-amino- 5-bromo-4-phenylthiazole (5.58 g, 96%). 1H NMR
[400 MHz, (CD3)2SO)] 7.28- 7.39 (3 H, m), 7.39-7.46 (2 H, m and 7.77-7.84
(2 H, m); m/z (ES +ve ion mode) 255.0 (MH+); (ES -ve ion mode)
253.1[(M-H)-], both for 79Br.
