(6a) A solution of NCS (30 mg, 0.21 mmol) in dry DMF (3 mL) was added
dropwise to a solution of 5a (56 mg, 0.21 mmol) in the same solvent (7
mL). The mixture was stirred at r.t. for 1 h, the solvent was removed
under reduced pressure, and the residue was purified by chromatography on
silica gel (10 g) with CH2Cl2 as eluent, which afforded 6a. White solid,
yield 60 mg, 95%. mp 188- 190 °C. IR (KBr): 3407, 3062, 1699, 1642, 1559,
1508, 1475, 1451, 1422, 1365, 1246, 1057, 799, 760, 641 cm-1. 1H NMR
(DMSO-d6): δ = 1.55-1.66 (dt, 1 H, J(t) = 12.30 Hz, J(d) = 7.52 Hz, 2' β
-H), 2.36-2.47 (dt, 1 H, J(t) = 12.30 Hz, J(d) = 7.14 Hz, 2' α -H),
3.37-3.43 (m, 1 H, 1' β -H), 3.70-3.79 (part A of an ABM system ABM, JAB
= 13.35 Hz, JAM = 9.26 Hz, CHHN), 4.21-4.29 (part B of an ABM system ABM,
JBA = 13.35 Hz, JBM = 5.40 Hz, CHHN), 4.93-5.01 (m, 1 H, 3' β -H),
5.37-5.40 (d, 1 H, J = 5.53 Hz, OH exchangeable with D2O), 7.24-7.36 (m,
4 H, ArH), 8.13 (s, 1 H, 6-H), 11.85 (br s, 1 H, NH exchangeable with
D2O). 13C NMR (DMSO-d6): δ = 40.51 (CH2), 40.99 (CH), 52.51 (CH2), 73.13
(CH), 106.39 (C), 123.99, 124.71, 127.51 and 127.86 (CH), 142.42 (C),
143.11 (CH), 147.10 (C), 150.66 (C), 159.80 (C). Anal. Calcd for
C14H13ClN2O3: C, 57.44; H, 4.48; N, 9.57. Found: C, 57.35; H, 4.59; N,
9.71.
